    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Changes\n\nThe identity key was a plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` string; I redesigned it to the spec's v2 form and updated the two detection paths that depend on it.\n\n**New `Soundex` helper** \u2014 `model/Soundex.java`: a standard American Soundex implementation (initial letter + three digits, correctly handling h/w bridging vs. vowel separation), placed alongside the existing `Sha256`/`Luhn` domain helpers so phonetic name coding lives in one reusable place.\n\n**`Owner.getIdentityKey()`** \u2014 now returns `Sha256.hex(normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + Soundex.of(lastName))`, i.e. a 64-char hex digest. `householdId` is no longer part of the key. Since the stored telephone/email are already normalized/lower-cased at creation, the key is consistent on every later read.\n\n**`PossibleDuplicateDetector`** (soft match) \u2014 the trigger changed from *\"exact last name + postcode + different telephone\"* to *\"Soundex(lastName) matches + postcode matches + identity key differs\"*. It now iterates `findAllOwners()` instead of the prefix `findByLastName`, because a phonetic match can span different spellings the prefix query would miss. Deleted owners are still ignored.\n\n**Behavioral consequences (as specified):**\n- Duplicate detection (409) is now the single identity key \u2014 the email-domain blocklist still runs first (controller order unchanged), deleted owners are still ignored.\n- Two owners with the same last name + postcode but **different telephones** now get **different** identity keys \u2192 no longer a hard 409; instead they're created and flagged as a soft match.\n- The separate household-derived 409 path is gone, since `householdId` is no longer in the key. `householdId` itself is still generated and exposed (household size, membership cap, etc. are untouched).\n\nI also refreshed the now-stale docs to match: the `DuplicateOwnerValidator`/`DuplicateOwnerException` javadocs, `Owner.getPossibleDuplicate()`, and the OpenAPI `identityKey` / `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` field descriptions.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical identity \u2192 409) both green, BUILD SUCCESS.",
